  <p>
    The set emits <code>nudge:start</code>, <code>nudge:complete</code> and <code>nudge:cancelled</code>; the reel itself emits <code>phase:enter</code> and <code>phase:exit</code> with the name <code>'nudge'</code>. <code>skipNudge()</code> jumps straight to the
    landed state. See the <a href="/guides/nudge/">nudge guide</a> and the <a href="/recipes/nudge/">nudge recipes</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Per-reel geometry</h2>

  <p>
    Reels in one set do not all have to be the same length; a pyramid board
    has a short reel at each side and a tall one in the middle. Four values
    per reel describe that, and the motion layer reads them rather than
    assuming a uniform grid.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose my-4 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
