  <Callout kind="remember">
    A reel is an array that is longer than the window. Its only state is how
    far it has travelled; every position is index times pitch plus the
    remainder, and the wrap count is travel divided by pitch. Phases set
    speeds, the motion layer turns speed into travel, and the stop feeds the
    landing ids in one per wrap until the strip is the frame.
  </Callout>
</Architecture>
